---
import DefaultLayout from "../../layouts/DefaultLayout.astro";

// This page describes the data that the API and site collect. Keep it in step
// with the code: auth.py (Clerk, IP addresses), limits.py (usage.db), api.py
// (sessions in memory), and DefaultLayout.astro (third-party fonts). A change
// to any of those may need a change here and a new EFFECTIVE_DATE.
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "October 31, 2026";
const CONTACT_EMAIL = "mmortondeveloper@gmail.com";

const processors = [
  {
    name: "Clerk",
    role: "runs sign-in and stores your account",
    href: "https://clerk.com/legal/privacy",
  },
  {
    name: "Anthropic",
    role: "the Claude API, which answers chat questions",
    href: "https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy",
  },
  {
    name: "Cloudflare",
    role: "serves the site and forwards requests to the API",
    href: "https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/",
  },
  {
    name: "Google Cloud",
    role: "hosts the API (Cloud Run) and keeps its request logs",
    href: "https://cloud.google.com/terms/cloud-privacy-notice",
  },
  {
    name: "Google Fonts",
    role: "serves the site's fonts, so your browser contacts Google",
    href: "https://policies.google.com/privacy",
  },
];
---

<DefaultLayout title="Privacy">
  <article class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-bone">
    <h1 class="font-pixel text-lg sm:text-2xl text-ember leading-tight">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="text-mist">Effective {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

    <p>
      Warlock is a free rules assistant for the D&D System Reference Document.
      It collects as little as it can. This page says what it does collect, why,
      who else sees it, and how long it is kept.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-pixel text-xs text-ember mt-4">What we collect</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 flex flex-col gap-2">
      <li>
        <strong>Your account, if you sign in.</strong> Clerk stores your email
        address and, if you sign in with another service such as Google, the
        name and profile picture it shares. Our server only ever sees your Clerk
        user ID.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your IP address, if you chat without signing in.</strong> We use
        it to give each anonymous visitor a fair daily allowance of questions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>How much you have used today.</strong> Each day we record how
        many tokens your questions used, against your user ID or IP address, so
        we can enforce the daily limit.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your chat questions.</strong> They are sent to Anthropic to be
        answered. Our server keeps a conversation in memory so follow-up
        questions make sense; it never writes them to disk.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your Discover searches.</strong> These are part of the request
        address, so they appear in our hosting providers' request logs.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ordinary request details.</strong> Like any website, our hosting
        providers see your IP address, browser type and the pages you request.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      We do not use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies. The only cookies
      are the ones Clerk needs to keep you signed in. We do not sell or share
      your information for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-pixel text-xs text-ember mt-4">Who else sees it</h2>
    <p>These services process data on our behalf:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 flex flex-col gap-2">
      {processors.map((processor) => (
        <li>
          <a href={processor.href} class="text-bone hover:text-ember">
            {processor.name}
          </a>
          , which {processor.role}.
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p>
      Anthropic does not train its models on questions sent through its API. We
      may also disclose information if the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-pixel text-xs text-ember mt-4">How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 flex flex-col gap-2">
      <li>Conversations: until the server restarts.</li>
      <li>
        Usage counts and the IP addresses or user IDs they belong to: until the
        server is redeployed.
      </li>
      <li>Request logs: as long as our hosting providers keep them.</li>
      <li>Your account: until you delete it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-pixel text-xs text-ember mt-4">Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can use Chat and Discover without an account. If you have one, you can
      edit or delete it from the account menu at the top right. To ask what we
      hold about you or to have it removed, email{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-bone hover:text-ember">
        {CONTACT_EMAIL}
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      Browsers can send a "Do Not Track" signal. We do not respond to it,
      because we do not track you across other sites in the first place.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-pixel text-xs text-ember mt-4">Children</h2>
    <p>
      Warlock is not meant for children under 13, and we do not knowingly
      collect information from them. If you believe a child has signed up, email
      us and we will delete the account.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-pixel text-xs text-ember mt-4">About the answers</h2>
    <p>
      Answers are written by an AI model and can be wrong. Check any rule
      against the cited SRD page before relying on it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-pixel text-xs text-ember mt-4">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, we will update it here and change the effective
      date above.
    </p>
  </article>
</DefaultLayout>
